  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Scattered showers and a few storms into Friday in\nthe Piedmont. \n\nFront across the Piedmont allowing for some convection early\nthis morning east of Lynchburg. Another wave arrives later this\nmorning and should provide a focus for more scattered\nshowers/few storms mainly along/east of Lynchburg to Danville \nto Reidsville. Should see drier air finally kick the precip east\nafter midday.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Clearing for the weekend; turning breezy and\ncooler. \n\nLingering upper level trough may produce cloudiness over WV and\nthe VA Highlands into the weekend with some sprinkles or \nflurries, but for the most part expecting a drying trend over \nthe weekend and into next week. Winds will also increase as \ncooler air advects into the region Friday night. \n\nIn general expecting near normal temperatures this weekend then \nmoderating early next week.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3: Mainly dry next week with moderating\ntemperatures before late week tumble.\n\nModel ensembles are in general agreement for dry conditions next \nweek and moderating temperatures. There are some differences \nwith respect to a southern stream feature that may pass well \nsouth of the area but it looks as though it will remain \nsuppressed to along the Gulf coast with cloud/rain impacts to \nSouth Texas and across the Gulf towards Florida. Late in the \nweek a northern stream trough is progged to drop south from \nCanada, passing over the Great Lakes. Track of this feature may \nbring a shot of cold air to our region by the following \nweekend...but no significant QPF is advertised attm.",
